      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LOUD (9) returns for the Reynolds yard and while she hasn't done a lot of winning, she finds a thin race to kick off the prep. Has placed twice fresh and has enough early muster to take advantage of the inside pillar. Can make a bold return. ROMAN MISS (6) has mixed her form since resuming but her peaks measure up. Gets a key booking in Gallagher and is another that is drawn well. Gets her chance to break a long run of outs. JOHNNY BOZ (5) turned in a good performance last time over 900m at Coonabarabran, finishing fifth after he got a long way back in the run. The extra journey should play into his hands. Poses a genuine threat. POWDERFINGER (4) never looked likely last start at Dubbo when getting too far back but has produced a couple of good efforts this prep that can give this a shake. Up to this. NOTABADCHASSIS (3) turned things around last start and landed the prize by 1.2 lengths over 1100m at Carinda. Solid top-three prospects.",
